# API design

- Use correct HTTP verbs: `GET` read, `POST` create, `PUT` replace, `PATCH` partial update, `DELETE` delete
- No `PUT` for partial update — use `PATCH`
- Business failures use proper 4xx (`400/401/403/404/409/422`), not HTTP 200
- Important write endpoints should support `Idempotency-Key` (payment/order-like operations)
- API versioning via URL prefix (`/v1/...`) or `Accept` header — not `?version=1`
- Errors must be structured and consistent (include `requestId`)

